_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNjA5NDQyMDYy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:shaders","name":"topic:shaders","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-06-14T04:38:44Z","updated_at":"2025-06-16T11:42:22Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.4.1 stable\n\n### System information\n\nLinux Mint 22.1 - Godot 4.4.1 Stable\n\n### Issue description\n\nDrag and click with the mouse to edit a value like a slider causes one of the following depending on the type of node in the Visualshader editor:\n\n**a) FloatConstant node/ Vector3Constant node:** The expected behavior, Mouse cursor is hidden and captured to the current position, dragging allows you to edit the value, releasing click leaves the mouse in the position where drag started.\n\n**b) ParameterNodes with Default value enabled:** Mouse is not captured, dragging the value only increases it one step before releasing the mouse without releasing the click button.\n\n**c) Nodes that spawn a secondary popup to edit values:** Mouse is captured, drag and slide functions correctly, releasing click teleports mouse to upper left corner of the screen (probably global coordinates instead of original node local coordinates)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nAdding those types of nodes in Visualshader editor and drag and slide to edit input fields like other input field in the inspector.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107521/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"la